  "known_security_and_rights": [
    "Torchvision 0.29.2 official release fixes unsafe tar archive extraction and checks on CPU ops; no broad safety guarantee.",
    "PyPI Linux torch 2.14.1 default wheel declares CUDA packages; do not reuse its SHA or size as the official +cpu wheel.",
    "PyTorch CPU index hashes are publisher-provided SHA256 URL fragments, not locally verified wheel bytes.",
    "TorchCodec uses system FFmpeg and its licenses; evaluate actual shared library variants, codecs and the right to redistribute.",
    "Num2words 0.5.14 is LGPL while the four model checkpoints are published as Apache-2.0; their licenses must not be conflated.",
    "torch, torchvision, torchcodec source Git commits are version provenance; they are not package SHA256."
  ],
  "verification_plan": {
    "H": "One explicit CPU-only reference profile with a single video backend can support metadata-level compatibility of the four selected small models while avoiding duplicate GPU stacks and alternate decoders.",
    "T": "Check official version compatibility and immutable source tag, wheel index sha256 for Linux x86_64 and Windows amd64; after separate approval, test at least 3 local inputs per task in network-denied sandbox, with validated decoder and stable output schema. Stop on missing license, hash, OS/ABI or any unauthorized fetch.",
    "D": "METADATA_PASS only when all version tags, wheel source hashes and package relations are coherent. DEPLOYMENT_PASS requires full dependency closure, model file integrity, four smoke tests, no external network access and RAM below limit. Any missing hardware/FFmpeg yields UNCERTAIN, not PASS.",
    "C": "Pytorch CPU backend may lack desired BF16 acceleration; incompatible native extensions or FFmpeg libraries may break the shared stack. Default pyav selection may silently defeat torchcodec-only packaging.",
